<file path=".github/DISCUSSION_TEMPLATE/welcome.md">
 1: # 🛡️ Welcome to the nftban Community!
 2: 
 3: nftban is a modern, modular Linux firewall framework built around nftables, Fail2Ban, and intelligent automation. We use GitHub Discussions as our main place to connect, share, and collaborate with sysadmins, security engineers, and testers.
 4: 
 5: ---
 6: 
 7: ## 💬 What You Can Do Here
 8: 
 9: - **Ask questions** about installation, configuration, and tuning on Debian, Ubuntu, RHEL, Rocky, Alma, or Fedora
10: - **Share ideas** or feature proposals that improve security, automation, or usability
11: - **Post results** from beta testing, performance benchmarking, or module experiments
12: - **Engage with others** — exchange best practices and security insights
13: - **Help improve nftban** by discussing architecture or suggesting code optimizations
14: 
15: ---
16: 
17: ## 🧩 Community Principles
18: 
19: We keep things:
20: 
21: - **Professional and open** — respect Linux diversity and deployment environments
22: - **Transparent** — credit both human and AI contributions
23: - **Collaborative** — every tester and partner strengthens nftban's protection layer
24: 
25: ---
26: 
27: ## 🚀 Getting Started
28: 
29: ### Introduce Yourself!
30: 
31: Tell us:
32: - Your Linux environment (e.g., Debian 12, Ubuntu 24.04, RHEL 9)
33: - How you deploy nftban (CLI, automation, containers, etc.)
34: - Which modules you're exploring (DDoS, GeoIP, Feeds, Fail2Ban...)
35: - Any ideas you'd like to test or refine
36: 
37: 💡 **Tip for new contributors**: Discussions are ideal for brainstorming and testing feedback. Confirmed bugs should still go to [Issues](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/issues).
38: 
39: ---
40: 
41: ## 📌 Discussion Categories
42: 
43: ### 💡 Ideas & Feature Requests
44: Propose enhancements, new modules, or workflow improvements.
45: 
46: ### 🧪 Beta Testing & Feedback
47: Share v0.9.0 beta results, migration experiences, and observations.
48: 
49: ### 🙋 Q&A
50: Ask installation, configuration, and troubleshooting questions.
51: 
52: ### 📢 Announcements
53: Project updates, releases, and important changes (maintained by project team).
54: 
55: ### 🗣️ General
56: Everything else — show & tell, use cases, integrations, and community chat.
57: 
58: ---
59: 
60: ## 🔗 Quick Links
61: 
62: - **📚 Documentation**: [docs/](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/tree/main/docs)
63: - **🐛 Bug Reports**: [Issues](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/issues)
64: - **🛡️ Main Project**: [nftban Repository](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban)
65: - **🌐 Website**: [nftban.com](https://nftban.com)
66: 
67: ---
68: 
69: ## 💬 Community Guidelines
70: 
71: - **Be respectful** — treat all members professionally
72: - **Search first** — check if your question has been answered
73: - **Provide details** — include OS, version, commands, and outputs when asking questions
74: - **Stay on topic** — use appropriate categories
75: - **Give back** — help others when you can
76: 
