<file path=".github/SUPPORT.md">
  1: # Getting Support for NFTBan
  2: 
  3: Thank you for using NFTBan! This document will help you get the support you need.
  4: 
  5: ## 📖 Documentation First
  6: 
  7: Before asking for help, please check our documentation:
  8: 
  9: ### Quick Help
 10: 
 11: ```bash
 12: # CLI help system (fastest!)
 13: nftban help                  # All commands
 14: nftban <command> help        # Specific command
 15: 
 16: # Man page (complete reference)
 17: man nftban
 18: 
 19: # System diagnostics
 20: nftban health check
 21: ```
 22: 
 23: ### Documentation Resources
 24: 
 25: | Resource | Purpose | Link |
 26: |----------|---------|------|
 27: | **README** | Project overview and quick start | [README.md](../README.md) |
 28: | **Documentation Guide** | How to find information | [docs/README.md](../docs/README.md) |
 29: | **Architecture** | Technical design and internals | [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) |
 30: | **Security** | Security model and CVE advisories | [SECURITY.md](../SECURITY.md) |
 31: | **Changelog** | Version history and changes | [CHANGELOG.md](../CHANGELOG.md) |
 32: | **Contributing** | How to contribute | [CONTRIBUTING.md](../CONTRIBUTING.md) |
 33: 
 34: ## 🐛 Reporting Bugs
 35: 
 36: Found a bug? Please use our bug report template:
 37: 
 38: 1. Go to [Issues](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/issues/new/choose)
 39: 2. Select "🐛 Bug Report"
 40: 3. Fill in ALL required fields:
 41:    - NFTBan version (`nftban --version`)
 42:    - OS and kernel (`uname -a`)
 43:    - Output of `nftban health check`
 44:    - Relevant logs from `/var/log/nftban/`
 45:    - Steps to reproduce
 46: 
 47: **Important:** Mask sensitive data (real IPs, domains, keys) before posting!
 48: 
 49: ## 💡 Feature Requests
 50: 
 51: Have an idea? We'd love to hear it!
 52: 
 53: 1. Go to [Issues](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/issues/new/choose)
 54: 2. Select "💡 Feature Request"
 55: 3. Describe:
 56:    - What problem does it solve?
 57:    - Who would benefit?
 58:    - How should it work?
 59: 
 60: ## 💬 Questions and Discussions
 61: 
 62: For general questions, discussions, or community help:
 63: 
 64: **GitHub Discussions** (Recommended)
 65: - [Start a Discussion](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/discussions)
 66: - Categories:
 67:   - **Q&A** - Ask questions
 68:   - **Ideas** - Share ideas and feedback
 69:   - **Show and tell** - Share your NFTBan setup
 70: 
 71: ## 🔒 Security Vulnerabilities
 72: 
 73: **DO NOT** report security vulnerabilities publicly!
 74: 
 75: Instead:
 76: 1. Email: **security@nftban.com**
 77: 2. Include:
 78:    - Vulnerability description
 79:    - Steps to reproduce
 80:    - Potential impact
 81:    - Suggested fix (if any)
 82: 
 83: We will respond within 48 hours and work with you on a fix.
 84: 
 85: See [SECURITY.md](../SECURITY.md) for our full security policy.
 86: 
 87: ## 📧 Email Support
 88: 
 89: For other inquiries:
 90: - **General:** contact@nftban.com
 91: - **Security:** security@nftban.com
 92: 
 93: ## ⏱️ Response Times
 94: 
 95: We strive to respond within:
 96: - **Security issues:** 48 hours
 97: - **Critical bugs:** 72 hours
 98: - **Other issues:** 7 days
 99: - **Feature requests:** 14 days
100: 
101: **Note:** NFTBan is maintained by volunteers. Response times may vary.
102: 
103: ## 🚀 Commercial Support
104: 
105: Need priority support, custom features, or professional services?
106: 
107: Contact us at: **contact@nftban.com**
108: 
109: We offer:
110: - Priority bug fixes
111: - Custom feature development
112: - Professional installation and configuration
113: - Training and consulting
114: - SLA-backed support
115: 
116: ## 🤝 Community Guidelines
117: 
118: When asking for help:
119: 
120: ✅ **DO:**
121: - Search existing issues first
122: - Provide complete information
123: - Be patient and respectful
124: - Follow up on your issues
125: - Thank helpers
126: - Share solutions that worked
127: 
128: ❌ **DON'T:**
129: - Demand immediate responses
130: - Post the same question multiple times
131: - Share sensitive data publicly
132: - Be rude or aggressive
133: - Ignore requested information
134: 
135: ## 📚 Self-Help Resources
136: 
137: ### Common Issues
138: 
139: **"I locked myself out!"**
140: ```bash
141: # If you have console access:
142: sudo nftban firewall status
143: sudo nft list tables
144: # Check whitelist configuration
145: ```
146: 
147: **"Firewall not working"**
148: ```bash
149: # Run health check
150: nftban health check
151: 
152: # Check service status
153: systemctl status nftban
154: journalctl -u nftban -n 50
155: ```
156: 
157: **"Ban command not working"**
158: ```bash
159: # Check if IP is whitelisted
160: nftban search <ip>
161: nftban whitelist list
162: ```
163: 
164: ### Diagnostic Commands
165: 
166: ```bash
167: # System health
168: nftban health check
169: 
170: # Firewall status
171: nftban firewall status
172: nft list tables
173: nft list table inet nftban_main
174: 
175: # Logs
176: journalctl -u nftban -n 100
177: tail -f /var/log/nftban/*.log
178: 
179: # Version info
180: nftban --version
181: nft --version
182: uname -a
183: ```
184: 
185: ## 🌐 External Resources
186: 
187: - **Website:** https://nftban.com
188: - **GitHub:** https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban
189: - **nftables Wiki:** https://wiki.nftables.org/
190: - **Fail2ban Docs:** https://fail2ban.readthedocs.io/
191: 
192: ## 🎓 Learning Resources
193: 
194: **For Users:**
195: 1. Read [README.md](../README.md) - 30 minutes
196: 2. Try `nftban help` - Interactive learning
197: 3. Read `man nftban` - Complete reference
198: 
199: **For Admins:**
200: 1. Read [ARCHITECTURE.md](../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) - 2 hours
201: 2. Study [SECURITY.md](../SECURITY.md) - Security model
202: 3. Explore `/usr/lib/nftban/` - Source code
203: 
204: ## 📊 Issue Priority
205: 
206: We prioritize issues based on:
207: 
208: 1. **Critical:** Security vulnerabilities, data loss, system crashes
209: 2. **High:** Major functionality broken, production impact
210: 3. **Medium:** Feature not working as expected
211: 4. **Low:** Minor bugs, cosmetic issues
212: 5. **Enhancement:** New features, improvements
213: 
214: ## ✅ What Makes a Good Issue?
215: 
216: **Good Example:**
217: ```
218: Title: [BUG] Ban command crashes when no arguments provided
219: 
220: NFTBan Version: 0.31.1
221: OS: Rocky Linux 9.3
222: Kernel: 6.1.0
223: 
224: Steps to reproduce:
225: 1. Run: nftban ban
226: 2. Expected: Usage message
227: 3. Actual: unbound variable error
228: 
229: Output: [paste error]
230: Health check: [paste output]
231: ```
232: 
233: **Bad Example:**
234: ```
235: Title: not working
236: 
237: it doesnt work help
238: ```
239: 
240: ## 🙏 Thank You!
241: 
242: Your questions, bug reports, and feedback help make NFTBan better for everyone.
243: 
244: We appreciate your time and patience! 🎉
245: 
246: ---
247: 
248: **NFTBan Project** - Simplifying Linux Firewall Management
