237: # HELP
238: # =============================================================================
239: 
240: 
241: nftban_geoban_help() {
242:     cat <<'EOF'
243: GeoBan Country Blocking
244: 
245: Usage:
246:   nftban geoban ban <CC> [CC...]           # Ban country traffic
247:   nftban geoban unban <CC> [CC...]         # Remove country ban
248:   nftban geoban whitelist <CC> [CC...]     # Whitelist country (allow)
249:   nftban geoban unwhitelist <CC> [CC...]   # Remove country whitelist
250:   nftban geoban list                       # List active country blocks
251:   nftban geoban status                     # Show GeoBan status
252:   nftban geoban update                     # Update all active countries
253:   nftban geoban config                     # Show GeoBan configuration
254:   nftban geoban help                       # Show this help
255: 
256: Country Codes:
257:   Use ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes (2 letters, uppercase)
258:   Examples: CN (China), RU (Russia), US (United States), GB (United Kingdom)
259: 
260: Examples:
261:   nftban geoban ban CN RU              # Block China and Russia
262:   nftban geoban whitelist US GB        # Allow USA and UK
263:   nftban geoban list                   # Show active blocks
264:   nftban geoban unban CN               # Remove China block
265:   nftban geoban status                 # Check GeoBan status
266: 
267: Features:
268:   • Atomic Operations: Zero-downtime updates via netlink
269:   • RIR Data Sources: ARIN, RIPE, APNIC, LACNIC, AFRINIC
270:   • ETag Caching: Reduces bandwidth and API rate limits
271:   • CIDR Merging: Optimizes memory footprint
272:   • Safety Limits: CPU/RAM monitoring prevents system overload
273: 
274: Notes:
275:   • GeoBan uses the nftban-geoip Go binary for performance
276:   • Changes are applied atomically to running firewall
277:   • Country IP lists are cached in /var/cache/nftban/geoban/
278:   • Configuration files stored in /etc/nftban/geoban.d/
279: 
280: EOF
281: }
282: 
283: # Export the main function
284: # Exit marker for testing validation
285: command -v nftban_cmd_exit >/dev/null 2>&1 && nftban_cmd_exit "geoban"
