 953: 
 954:     # Send test alert
 955:     nftban login test
 956: 
 957:     # View recent logs
 958:     nftban login logs 100
 959: 
 960: CONFIGURATION:
 961:     /etc/nftban/conf.d/login_alert.conf
 962: 
 963:     Key settings:
 964:     - NFTBAN_LOGIN_ALERT_ENABLED: Enable/disable alerts
 965:     - NFTBAN_LOGIN_ALERT_EMAIL: Destination email address
 966:     - NFTBAN_LOGIN_ALERT_GEOIP: Include GeoIP information
 967:     - NFTBAN_LOGIN_ALERT_FORMAT: html or text
 968:     - LOGIN_FAIL_THRESHOLD: Failed attempts before ban (default: 5)
 969:     - LOGIN_FAIL_WINDOW: Time window in seconds (default: 300)
 970: 
 971: SYSTEMD SERVICE:
 972:     Service: ${NFTBAN_SERVICE_LOGIN_MONITOR:-nftban-login-monitor.service}
 973:     Status:  systemctl status nftban-login-monitor
 974:     Logs:    journalctl -u nftban-login-monitor -f
 975: 
 976: For more information: https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/CLI-Commands-Reference
 977: 
 978: nftban — Simplifying Linux Firewall Management
