<file path="packaging/systemd/nftban-firewall-init.service">
 1: [Unit]
 2: Description=NFTBan Firewall Initialization (with startup delay)
 3: Documentation=man:nftban(8)
 4: After=network-online.target nftables.service
 5: Wants=network-online.target
 6: # NOTE: Don't use Before=sshd.service (would delay SSH)
 7: 
 8: [Service]
 9: Type=forking
10: RemainAfterExit=yes
11: 
12: # CRITICAL: Set environment variable to enable 5-minute startup delay
13: Environment="NFTBAN_SYSTEMD_BOOT=1"
14: 
15: # Set PATH to ensure we find nft command (works on RHEL, Debian, Ubuntu)
16: Environment="PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
17: 
18: # Run as root (firewall init requires root privileges)
19: User=root
20: Group=root
21: 
22: # Load config file for NFTBAN_STARTUP_DELAY value
23: EnvironmentFile=-/etc/nftban/nftban.conf
24: 
25: # FIX: Only load snapshot if startup delay is 0 (disabled)
26: # If delay is enabled, let 'nftban firewall init' handle everything after the delay
27: # This ensures the delay actually works as intended
28: ExecStartPre=-/bin/bash -c 'if [ "${NFTBAN_STARTUP_DELAY:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then \
29:     command -v nft >/dev/null 2>&1 && nft -f /var/lib/nftban/snapshots/last.nft 2>/dev/null || true; \
30: fi'
31: 
32: # Initialize firewall (synchronous execution when delay is set)
33: # If delay=0: Run in background for fast boot
34: # If delay>0: Run synchronously so delay happens before firewall loads
35: ExecStart=/bin/bash -c 'if [ "${NFTBAN_STARTUP_DELAY:-0}" -eq 0 ]; then \
36:     /usr/sbin/nftban firewall init &; \
37: else \
38:     /usr/sbin/nftban firewall init; \
39: fi'
40: 
41: # NOTE: Snapshot save will be done by snapshot timer (not here)
42: 
43: # On stop, flush firewall (safety measure)
44: ExecStop=/bin/sh -c 'command -v nft >/dev/null 2>&1 && nft flush ruleset || true'
45: 
46: # Don't restart on failure (would cause loops)
47: Restart=no
48: 
49: # Security hardening (minimal - service needs root for firewall ops)
50: PrivateTmp=yes
51: ProtectHome=yes
52: NoNewPrivileges=no
53: # Note: Cannot use ProtectSystem=strict (needs to write to /var/lib/nftban)
54: ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/nftban /var/log/nftban /var/cache/nftban /run/nftban
55: 
56: [Install]
57: WantedBy=multi-user.target
</file>

<file path="packaging/INSTALLATION_REMOVAL_VERIFICATION.md">
  1: # NFTBan UI v0.5.1 - Installation & Removal Verification
  2: 
  3: **Date**: 2025-11-16
  4: **Purpose**: Verify complete installation and clean removal for both RPM and DEB packages
  5: 
  6: ---
  7: 
  8: ## Installation Requirements Checklist
  9: 
 10: ### 1. Users and Groups
 11: 
 12: #### What Gets Created on Install?
 13: 
 14: | Item | Type | UID/GID | Home | Shell | Purpose |
 15: |------|------|---------|------|-------|---------|
 16: | `nftban` | User | System (auto) | /var/lib/nftban | /sbin/nologin | Service user |
 17: | `nftban` | Group | System (auto) | - | - | Daemon group (no human users) |
 18: | `nftban-cli` | Group | System (auto) | - | - | CLI and Web GUI operators |
 19: | `nftban-auditors` | Group | System (auto) | - | - | Read-only auditors |
 20: 
 21: > **Note:** NFTBan v1.0 uses 3-group model: `nftban` (daemon only), `nftban-cli` (CLI + Web GUI), `nftban-auditors` (read-only). The old `nftban-web` group is **retired**.
 22: 
 23: #### RPM Implementation (%pre)
 24: ```bash
 25: getent group nftban >/dev/null || groupadd -r nftban
 26: getent group nftban-auditors >/dev/null || groupadd -r nftban-auditors
 27: getent passwd nftban >/dev/null || \
 28:     useradd -r -g nftban -d /var/lib/nftban -s /sbin/nologin \
 29:     -c "NFTBan system user" nftban
 30: ```
 31: 
 32: #### DEB Implementation (postinst)
 33: ```bash
 34: if ! getent group nftban > /dev/null 2>&1; then
 35:     addgroup --system nftban
 36: fi
 37: if ! getent group nftban-auditors > /dev/null 2>&1; then
 38:     addgroup --system nftban-auditors
 39: fi
 40: if ! getent passwd nftban > /dev/null 2>&1; then
 41:     adduser --system --group --home /var/lib/nftban \
 42:         --no-create-home --disabled-login \
 43:         --gecos "NFTBan system user" nftban
 44: fi
 45: ```
 46: 
 47: **Status**: ✅ Identical behavior between RPM and DEB
 48: 
 49: ---
 50: 
 51: ### 2. Systemd Services
 52: 
 53: #### What Gets Installed?
 54: 
 55: | Service | Type | Enabled on Install? | Started on Install? |
 56: |---------|------|---------------------|---------------------|
 57: | `nftban-ui-auth.socket` | Socket | ✅ Yes (fresh install) | ✅ Yes (fresh install) |
 58: | `nftban-ui-auth.service` | Service | ⚠️ No (socket-activated) | ⚠️ No (on-demand) |
 59: | `nftban-ui.service` | Service | ⚠️ Manual | ⚠️ Manual |
 60: 
 61: **Note**: The auth service is socket-activated, so it starts automatically when the socket receives a connection.
 62: 
 63: #### RPM Implementation (%post)
 64: ```bash
 65: # Enable and start socket (will auto-start service on-demand)
 66: %systemd_post nftban-ui-auth.socket
 67: %systemd_post nftban-ui.service
 68: 
 69: # Only enable socket if this is initial install
 70: if [ $1 -eq 1 ]; then
 71:     systemctl enable nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
 72:     systemctl start nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
 73: fi
 74: 
 75: # If upgrading and service is already running, restart it
 76: if [ $1 -eq 2 ]; then
 77:     systemctl try-restart nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
 78:     systemctl try-restart nftban-ui.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
 79: fi
 80: ```
 81: 
 82: **$1 = 1**: Fresh install
 83: **$1 = 2**: Upgrade
 84: 
 85: #### DEB Implementation (postinst)
 86: ```bash
 87: # Enable and start socket on fresh install
 88: if [ -z "$2" ]; then
 89:     deb-systemd-helper enable nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null || true
 90:     deb-systemd-invoke start nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null || true
 91: fi
 92: 
 93: # Restart services on upgrade
 94: if [ -n "$2" ]; then
 95:     deb-systemd-invoke try-restart nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null || true
 96:     deb-systemd-invoke try-restart nftban-ui.service >/dev/null || true
 97: fi
 98: ```
 99: 
100: **$2 = ""**: Fresh install
101: **$2 = "old-version"**: Upgrade
102: 
103: **Status**: ✅ Identical behavior between RPM and DEB
104: 
105: ---
106: 
107: ### 3. Files and Directories
108: 
109: #### Binaries
110: 
111: | File | Path | Permissions | Owner | Group |
112: |------|------|-------------|-------|-------|
113: | GUI Server | /usr/sbin/nftban-ui | 0755 | root | root |
114: | Auth Service | /usr/libexec/nftban-ui-auth | 0755 | root | root |
115: 
116: #### Systemd Units
117: 
118: | File | Path | Permissions | Owner | Group |
119: |------|------|-------------|-------|-------|
120: | GUI Service | /usr/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui.service | 0644 | root | root |
121: | Auth Service | /usr/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui-auth.service | 0644 | root | root |
122: | Auth Socket | /usr/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui-auth.socket | 0644 | root | root |
123: 
124: **Note**: DEB uses `/lib/systemd/system/` which is symlinked to `/usr/lib/systemd/system/`
125: 
126: #### Configuration Files
127: 
128: | File | Path | Permissions | Owner | Group | Replaced on Upgrade? |
129: |------|------|-------------|-------|-------|---------------------|
130: | PAM Config | /etc/pam.d/nftban-ui | 0644 | root | root | ⚠️ No (noreplace/conffile) |
131: | Allowed Groups | /etc/nftban/allowed-gui-groups | 0644 | root | root | ⚠️ No (noreplace/conffile) |
132: | Main Config | /etc/nftban/ui.conf | 0644 | root | root | ⚠️ No (created by `nftban ui init`) |
133: | IP Whitelist | /etc/nftban/ui-whitelist.conf | 0644 | root | root | ⚠️ No (created by `nftban ui init`) |
134: 
135: **Note**: Config files marked with `config(noreplace)` in RPM and conffiles in DEB will NOT be overwritten on upgrade.
136: 
137: #### Runtime Directories
138: 
139: | Directory | Path | Permissions | Owner | Group | Created When? |
140: |-----------|------|-------------|-------|-------|--------------|
141: | Runtime Dir | /run/nftban-ui/ | 0755 | root | nftban | postinst |
142: | Socket | /run/nftban-ui/auth.sock | 0770 | root | nftban | systemd (socket activation) |
143: 
144: #### Log Directories
145: 
146: | Directory | Path | Permissions | Owner | Group | Created When? |
147: |-----------|------|-------------|-------|-------|--------------|
148: | Log Dir | /var/log/nftban/ | 0750 | nftban | nftban | Package install |
149: 
150: #### Data Directories
151: 
152: | Directory | Path | Permissions | Owner | Group | Purpose |
153: |-----------|------|-------------|-------|-------|---------|
154: | Web Files | /usr/share/nftban-ui/web/ | 0755 | root | root | Static HTML/CSS/JS |
155: | State Dir | /var/lib/nftban/ | 0755 | nftban | nftban | Runtime state (not created by package) |
156: 
157: ---
158: 
159: ## Removal Procedures Checklist
160: 
161: ### 1. Service Shutdown
162: 
163: #### What Happens on Package Removal?
164: 
165: **RPM (%preun)**:
166: ```bash
167: %systemd_preun nftban-ui.service
168: %systemd_preun nftban-ui-auth.socket
169: %systemd_preun nftban-ui-auth.service
170: ```
171: 
172: **Translation**:
173: ```bash
174: if [ $1 -eq 0 ]; then  # Only on removal, not upgrade
175:     systemctl stop nftban-ui.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
176:     systemctl stop nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
177:     systemctl stop nftban-ui-auth.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
178:     systemctl disable nftban-ui.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
179:     systemctl disable nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
180:     systemctl disable nftban-ui-auth.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
181: fi
182: ```
183: 
184: **$1 = 0**: Complete removal
185: **$1 = 1**: Upgrade (don't stop services)
186: 
187: **DEB (prerm)**:
188: ```bash
189: case "$1" in
190:     remove|deconfigure)
191:         deb-systemd-invoke stop nftban-ui.service >/dev/null || true
192:         deb-systemd-invoke stop nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null || true
193:         deb-systemd-invoke stop nftban-ui-auth.service >/dev/null || true
194:         ;;
195: esac
196: ```
197: 
198: **Status**: ✅ Both stop services before removal
199: 
200: ---
201: 
202: ### 2. File Cleanup
203: 
204: #### RPM: Files Removed Automatically
205: 
206: RPM automatically removes all files listed in `%files` section:
207: - ✅ `/usr/sbin/nftban-ui`
208: - ✅ `/usr/libexec/nftban-ui-auth`
209: - ✅ `/usr/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui*.service`
210: - ✅ `/usr/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui-auth.socket`
211: - ✅ `/usr/share/nftban-ui/`
212: 
213: #### RPM: Files NOT Removed (By Design)
214: 
215: **Config files marked with `config(noreplace)`**:
216: - ⚠️ `/etc/pam.d/nftban-ui` - **KEPT** (admin may have customized)
217: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/allowed-gui-groups` - **KEPT** (admin may have customized)
218: 
219: **Created at runtime (not in %files)**:
220: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/ui.conf` - **KEPT** (created by `nftban ui init`)
221: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/ui-whitelist.conf` - **KEPT** (contains admin's IPs)
222: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/ssl/` - **KEPT** (TLS certificates)
223: - ⚠️ `/var/log/nftban/*.log` - **KEPT** (audit trail)
224: - ⚠️ `/run/nftban-ui/` - **REMOVED** (tmpfs, disappears on reboot anyway)
225: 
226: #### RPM: %postun Cleanup
227: 
228: ```bash
229: %systemd_postun_with_restart nftban-ui.service
230: %systemd_postun_with_restart nftban-ui-auth.socket
231: ```
232: 
233: This runs `systemctl daemon-reload` to clean up systemd state.
234: 
235: ---
236: 
237: #### DEB: Files Removed Automatically
238: 
239: DEB automatically removes all installed files except conffiles:
240: - ✅ `/usr/sbin/nftban-ui`
241: - ✅ `/usr/libexec/nftban-ui-auth`
242: - ✅ `/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui*.service`
243: - ✅ `/lib/systemd/system/nftban-ui-auth.socket`
244: - ✅ `/usr/share/nftban-ui/`
245: 
246: #### DEB: Files NOT Removed on `apt remove`
247: 
248: **Configuration files (automatically preserved)**:
249: - ⚠️ `/etc/pam.d/nftban-ui` - **KEPT**
250: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/allowed-gui-groups` - **KEPT**
251: 
252: **Created at runtime**:
253: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/ui.conf` - **KEPT**
254: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/ui-whitelist.conf` - **KEPT**
255: - ⚠️ `/etc/nftban/ssl/` - **KEPT**
256: - ⚠️ `/var/log/nftban/*.log` - **KEPT**
257: 
258: #### DEB: Files Removed on `apt purge` (postrm with purge)
259: 
260: **Current DEB postrm**:
261: ```bash
262: case "$1" in
263:     purge)
264:         rm -rf /etc/nftban/ui.conf
265:         rm -rf /etc/nftban/ui-whitelist.conf
266:         rm -rf /etc/nftban/ssl
267:         rm -rf /var/log/nftban/ui-*.log
268:         rm -rf /run/nftban-ui
269: 
270:         deb-systemd-helper purge nftban-ui.service >/dev/null || true
271:         deb-systemd-helper purge nftban-ui-auth.socket >/dev/null || true
272:         deb-systemd-helper purge nftban-ui-auth.service >/dev/null || true
273:         ;;
274: esac
275: ```
276: 
277: **Status**: ✅ DEB purge removes runtime files
278: 
279: ---
280: 
281: ### 3. Users and Groups Cleanup
282: 
283: #### ⚠️ IMPORTANT: Users/Groups Are NOT Removed
284: 
285: **RPM**: No user/group cleanup in %postun
286: **DEB**: No user/group cleanup in postrm
287: 
288: **Why?**
289: 1. **Security**: UIDs/GIDs might be reused, causing permission issues
290: 2. **Data preservation**: User might own files outside package management
291: 3. **Best practice**: System users are rarely removed
292: 
293: **Manual cleanup** (if needed after uninstall):
294: ```bash
295: # WARNING: Only do this if you're sure!
296: userdel nftban
297: groupdel nftban
298: groupdel nftban-auditors
299: ```
300: 
301: ---
302: 
303: ## Current Issues Found
304: 
305: ### ❌ Issue 1: DEB postinst creates /run/nftban-ui on every install
306: **Problem**: /run is tmpfs, this directory should be created by systemd or the service itself
307: **Impact**: LOW - Directory will be recreated, but unnecessary
308: 
309: **Recommendation**: Remove from postinst, add to systemd service:
310: ```ini
311: [Service]
312: RuntimeDirectory=nftban-ui
313: RuntimeDirectoryMode=0755
314: ```
315: 
316: ### ❌ Issue 2: Log directory ownership
317: **RPM**: Creates directory in %files, sets ownership in %post
318: **DEB**: Creates directory in rules, sets ownership in postinst
319: 
320: **Problem**: Race condition - directory might not exist when setting ownership
321: 
322: **Recommendation**: Consistent approach:
323: ```bash
324: install -d -m 0750 -o nftban -g nftban /var/log/nftban
325: ```
326: 
327: ### ❌ Issue 3: RPM doesn't clean up generated configs on removal
328: **Current**: `/etc/nftban/ui.conf` and SSL certs left behind after `rpm -e`
329: **Expected**: Admin configs should be kept (correct behavior)
