353: 
354: ## 🔒 Post-Installation Security Configuration
355: 
356: ### GUI Port Access Control (CRITICAL)
357: 
358: After installing nftban-ui, you **MUST** configure nftables to restrict GUI port access (3940, 18443) to whitelisted IPs only.
359: 
360: #### Why This Is Critical
361: 
362: By default, the nftban_main chain has `policy accept`, which means:
363: - ✅ Whitelisted IPs: Full access (all ports)
364: - ⚠️ Other IPs: Can access GUI ports (SECURITY RISK)
365: 
366: The GUI should ONLY be accessible from whitelisted IPs.
367: 
368: #### Quick Fix (5 minutes)
369: 
370: ```bash
371: # 1. Backup current ruleset
372: nft list ruleset > /root/nftables-backup-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).nft
373: 
374: # 2. Change main chain policy to DROP
375: nft chain inet nftban_main input '{ policy drop ; }'
376: 
377: # 3. Add public service rules (SSH, HTTP, HTTPS)
378: nft add rule inet nftban_main input tcp dport 22 accept comment "SSH - public"
379: nft add rule inet nftban_main input tcp dport 80 accept comment "HTTP - public"
380: nft add rule inet nftban_main input tcp dport 443 accept comment "HTTPS - public"
381: 
382: # 4. Make persistent
383: nft list ruleset > /etc/nftables.conf
384: systemctl enable nftables
385: ```
386: 
387: #### Result After Fix
388: 
389: ```
390: Incoming connection to port 3940:
391: 
392: 1. From whitelisted IP (e.g., 192.0.2.122):
393:    Priority 0: In whitelist_v4 → ACCEPT ✅
394:    Result: ✅ GUI accessible
395: 
396: 2. From non-whitelisted IP (e.g., 1.2.3.4):
397:    Priority 0: Not in whitelist_v4 → Continue
398:                Not matching SSH/HTTP/HTTPS rules
399:                Hit policy: DROP ❌
400:    Result: ❌ GUI blocked (as intended)
401: ```
402: 
403: #### Safety Checklist
404: 
405: **BEFORE changing policy to drop**:
406: 
407: - [ ] You are SSH'd from a whitelisted IP
408: - [ ] Whitelist contains your IP (`nft list set inet nftban_main whitelist_v4`)
409: - [ ] You have console/out-of-band access (in case of lockout)
410: - [ ] Backup created
411: - [ ] Public service rules added (SSH at minimum)
412: 
413: **If you get locked out**:
414: ```bash
415: # Use console access
416: # Restore backup:
417: nft -f /root/nftables-backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.nft
418: 
419: # Or change policy back:
420: nft chain inet nftban_main input '{ policy accept ; }'
421: ```
422: 
423: #### Verification
424: 
425: ```bash
426: # Check policy
427: nft list chain inet nftban_main input | grep policy
428: # Expected: "policy drop"
429: 
430: # Check whitelist
431: nft list set inet nftban_main whitelist_v4
432: # Should contain your admin IP
433: 
434: # Test GUI access from whitelisted IP
435: curl -I https://your-server:3940/
436: # Expected: ✅ Connection succeeds
437: 
438: # Test from non-whitelisted IP (should fail)
439: # Expected: ❌ Connection timeout/refused
440: ```
441: 
442: #### Alternative: Explicit GUI Port Blocking (Not Recommended)
443: 
444: If you cannot use `policy drop`, you can explicitly block GUI ports:
445: 
446: ```bash
447: # Add AFTER whitelist rules
448: nft add rule inet nftban_main input tcp dport 3940 drop comment "GUI - whitelist only"
449: nft add rule inet nftban_main input tcp dport 18443 drop comment "GUI - whitelist only"
450: ```
451: 
452: ⚠️ **Warning**: This is less secure (default allow). Use `policy drop` whenever possible.
453: 
