254: ## [0.31.0] - 2025-11-05
255: 
256: ### 🚨 CRITICAL SECURITY RELEASE
257: 
258: **CVE-2024-NFTBAN-001** - Rule order vulnerability allowing blacklisted IPs to bypass firewall.
259: 
260: ### Fixed
261: 
262: #### Security - Rule Processing Order (CRITICAL)
263: - **CRITICAL:** Fixed nftables rule order - blacklist checks now run BEFORE port checks
264:   - **Issue:** In v0.31.0, port allow rules executed before blacklist drops
265:   - **Impact:** Blacklisted IPs could access SSH (port 22) and all allowed services
266:   - **Root Cause:** Port checks (`tcp dport @tcp_ports accept`) ran before blacklist checks
267:   - **Fix:** Reordered rules so blacklist drops execute first, then port allows
268:   - **Testing:** Verified on 5 lab servers - blacklist now properly blocks all traffic
269: 
270: ```nft
271: # v0.31.0 (VULNERABLE):
272: tcp dport @tcp_ports accept    ← Port 22 accepted FIRST
273: ip saddr @blacklist_v4 drop    ← NEVER REACHED!
274: 
275: # v0.31.0 (SECURE):
276: ip saddr @blacklist_v4 counter drop    ← Check blacklist FIRST
277: tcp dport @tcp_ports counter accept    ← Then allow ports
278: ```
279: 
280: #### nftables Architecture Fixes
281: - **Fixed:** Chain naming consistency (`input_main` → `input`)
282: - **Fixed:** Numeric priorities (now `-5` and `0` instead of `-310` and `-300`)
283: - **Fixed:** Default policy set to `drop` (secure by default)
284: - **Fixed:** Set name typo (`whitelist_ipv4` → `whitelist_v4`)
285: - **Fixed:** nftables syntax (counter must come before accept/drop)
286: 
287: #### CLI Improvements
288: - **Fixed:** `ban` command now checks whitelist BEFORE banning
289:   - Prevents accidental lockout by refusing to ban whitelisted IPs
290:   - Shows clear error message with which whitelist file contains the IP
291:   - Provides step-by-step instructions if override needed
292: - **Fixed:** `ban` and `unban` commands no longer crash with no arguments
293:   - Added validation: `ip="${1:-}"` with `shift || true`
294:   - Shows usage message instead of "unbound variable" error
295: - **Fixed:** `nftban ban help` now shows help instead of trying to ban "help"
296: - **Added:** `nftban unban help` command for usage information
297: 
298: #### Performance Improvements
299: - **Fixed:** `feeds enable` command no longer blocks CLI
300:   - Feed download now runs in background with `disown`
301:   - Returns immediately with status message
302:   - User can check progress with `nftban feeds status`
303:   - Logs available at `/var/log/nftban/feeds.log`
304: 
305: ### Added
306: 
307: #### Monitoring & Observability
308: - **Added:** Packet counters to all nftables rules for traffic analysis
309: - **Added:** Comprehensive security warning when attempting to ban whitelisted IPs
310: 
311: ### Security
