<file path="VERSIONING.md">
  1: # NFTBan Versioning System
  2: 
  3: **Single Source of Truth:** All version numbers come from the `VERSION` file.
  4: 
  5: ## How It Works
  6: 
  7: ```
  8: VERSION file (1.0.5)
  9:     ├─→ Go binaries    (injected via ldflags during build)
 10:     ├─→ Bash scripts   (read from cli/lib/nftban/lib/version.sh)
 11:     ├─→ RPM packages   (read by packaging/build_nftban.sh)
 12:     ├─→ DEB packages   (read by packaging/build_nftban.sh)
 13:     └─→ GitHub Actions (read during release workflow)
 14: ```
 15: 
 16: ## The VERSION File
 17: 
 18: **Location:** `/VERSION`
 19: 
 20: **Content:** Single line with version number (no 'v' prefix)
 21: 
 22: ```
 23: 1.0.5
 24: ```
 25: 
 26: That's it! One file, one line, one truth.
 27: 
 28: ## Making a Release
 29: 
 30: ### Option 1: Bump Version Automatically (Recommended)
 31: 
 32: ```bash
 33: # Bump patch version (1.0.5 → 1.0.6)
 34: ./scripts/bump-version.sh patch
 35: 
 36: # Bump minor version (1.0.5 → 1.1.0)
 37: ./scripts/bump-version.sh minor
 38: 
 39: # Bump major version (1.0.5 → 2.0.0)
 40: ./scripts/bump-version.sh major
 41: 
 42: # Set specific version
 43: ./scripts/bump-version.sh 1.2.3
 44: ```
 45: 
 46: ### Option 2: Manual Update
 47: 
 48: ```bash
 49: # Edit VERSION file
 50: echo "1.0.6" > VERSION
 51: 
 52: # Commit
 53: git add VERSION
 54: git commit -m "chore: Bump version to 1.0.6"
 55: ```
 56: 
 57: ### Option 3: Tag and Release
 58: 
 59: ```bash
 60: # After bumping version, create a tag
 61: git tag v1.0.6 -m "Release v1.0.6"
 62: 
 63: # Push tag (triggers GitHub release workflow)
 64: git push origin v1.0.6
 65: ```
 66: 
 67: **The release workflow automatically:**
 68: 1. Reads version from `VERSION` file
 69: 2. Builds all packages
 70: 3. Creates GitHub Release
 71: 4. Uploads packages to release
 72: 5. Makes them available at download URLs
 73: 
 74: ## No More Manual Updates!
 75: 
 76: **Before (BAD):** Update version in 50+ files manually
 77: ```
 78: pkg/version/version.go
 79: cli/lib/nftban/lib/version.sh
 80: packaging/build_nftban.sh
 81: ... 47 more files
 82: ```
 83: 
 84: **After (GOOD):** Update ONE file
 85: ```
 86: VERSION
 87: ```
 88: 
 89: ## Where Versions Are Used
 90: 
 91: ### 1. Go Binaries
 92: 
 93: **Injected during build:**
 94: ```bash
 95: ./build.sh
 96: # Reads VERSION file
 97: # Builds with: -ldflags "-X github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/pkg/version.Version=1.0.5"
 98: ```
 99: 
100: **Usage in code:**
101: ```go
102: import "github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/pkg/version"
103: 
104: fmt.Println(version.Version)     // "1.0.5"
105: fmt.Println(version.FullVersion()) // "v1.0.5"
106: ```
107: 
108: ### 2. Bash Scripts
109: 
110: **Auto-loaded from VERSION file:**
111: ```bash
112: source "${NFTBAN_LIB_DIR}/lib/version.sh"
113: echo "$NFTBAN_VERSION"  # Reads from VERSION file automatically
114: ```
115: 
116: ### 3. RPM/DEB Packages
117: 
118: **Auto-read during packaging:**
119: ```bash
120: cd packaging
121: ./build_nftban.sh rpm  # Reads VERSION file
122: ./build_nftban.sh deb  # Reads VERSION file
123: ```
124: 
125: ### 4. GitHub Actions
126: 
127: **Read from VERSION file during workflows:**
128: ```yaml
129: - name: Get version
130:   run: |
131:     VERSION=$(cat VERSION)
132:     echo "Building version: $VERSION"
133: ```
134: 
135: ## Testing Version System
136: 
137: ```bash
138: # Test bash version reading
139: source cli/lib/nftban/lib/version.sh
140: echo "$NFTBAN_VERSION"
141: 
142: # Test Go version injection
143: ./build.sh
144: ./bin/nftban-core --version
145: 
146: # Test packaging version
147: cd packaging
148: ./build_nftban.sh rpm
149: # Check RPM version: rpm -qpi build/packages/RPMS/*/*.rpm | grep Version
150: ```
151: 
152: ## Migration Notes
153: 
154: **Old System:**
155: - Version hardcoded in multiple places
156: - Manual updates error-prone
157: - Easy to miss files
158: - Inconsistent versions possible
159: 
160: **New System:**
161: - Single VERSION file
162: - Automatic propagation
163: - Impossible to have inconsistent versions
164: - One command to bump version
165: 
166: ## Semantic Versioning
167: 
168: We follow [SemVer](https://semver.org/):
169: 
170: - **MAJOR** (1.x.x): Breaking changes
171: - **MINOR** (x.1.x): New features (backward compatible)
172: - **PATCH** (x.x.1): Bug fixes
173: 
174: ## Quick Reference
175: 
176: | Task | Command |
177: |------|---------|
178: | Check current version | `cat VERSION` |
179: | Bump patch | `./scripts/bump-version.sh patch` |
180: | Bump minor | `./scripts/bump-version.sh minor` |
181: | Bump major | `./scripts/bump-version.sh major` |
182: | Set specific version | `./scripts/bump-version.sh 1.2.3` |
183: | Create release | `git tag v$(cat VERSION) && git push origin v$(cat VERSION)` |
184: 
185: ## Summary
186: 
187: **Before each release:**
188: 1. `./scripts/bump-version.sh patch` (or minor/major)
189: 2. `git add VERSION && git commit -m "chore: Bump version to X.Y.Z"`
190: 3. `git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z`
191: 
192: **That's it!** All packages will be built with the correct version automatically.
</file>

