 66:     source "${NFTBAN_LIB_DIR}/core/nftban_output.sh"
 67: 
 68:     # Show standard banner
 69:     nftban_banner
 70: 
 71:     cat <<'HELP'
 72: 
 73: USAGE:
 74:     nftban portscan <command> [options]
 75: 
 76: COMMANDS:
 77:     enable              Enable port scan detection
 78:     disable             Disable port scan detection
 79:     status              Show detection status and configuration
 80:     check               Run manual port scan check (parse logs)
 81:     history             Show detected scans (last 24 hours)
 82:     test                Test port scan detection rules
 83:     help                Show this help message
 84: 
 85: DESCRIPTION:
 86:     The port scan detection module identifies IP addresses that access
 87:     multiple ports within a time window and automatically bans them
 88:     to prevent reconnaissance attacks.
 89: 
 90: HOW IT WORKS:
 91: 
 92:     1. Detection: Monitors nftables logs for connection attempts
 93:     2. Tracking: Records which ports each IP accesses
 94:     3. Threshold: Flags IPs accessing N ports in M seconds
 95:     4. Auto-Ban: Automatically bans detected scanners (if enabled)
 96: 
 97: DETECTION PARAMETERS:
 98: 
 99:     PORTSCAN_TIME_WINDOW="300"       # Time window (5 minutes)
100:     PORTSCAN_THRESHOLD="10"          # Ports to trigger detection
101:     PORTSCAN_DIVERSITY="true"        # Require port diversity
102:     PORTSCAN_AUTO_BAN="true"         # Auto-ban detected scanners
103: 
104: MONITORING MODES:
105: 
106:     "closed"  - Monitor only closed ports (RECOMMENDED)
107:                 ✅ Detects reconnaissance scans
108:                 ✅ No false positives from legitimate traffic
109:                 ✅ Best for most servers
110: 
111:     "all"     - Monitor all ports (AGGRESSIVE)
112:                 ⚠️  May cause false positives
113:                 ✅ Detects all scan types
114:                 ⚠️  Only use if under active attack
115: 
116:     "custom"  - Monitor specific ports
117:                 ✅ Targeted protection
118:                 ✅ Flexible configuration
119:                 Set PORTSCAN_CUSTOM_PORTS="1-1024,3306,5432"
120: 
121: BAN SETTINGS:
122: 
123:     PORTSCAN_AUTO_BAN="true"         # Enable auto-banning
124:     PORTSCAN_BAN_TYPE="temporary"    # Ban type (temporary/permanent)
125:     PORTSCAN_BAN_TIME="3600"         # Ban duration (1 hour)
126: 
127:     Examples:
128:       • Temporary ban: 1 hour cooling-off period
129:       • Permanent ban: Requires manual unban
130: 
131: CONFIGURATION:
132:     Port scan detection is configured in:
133:       /etc/nftban/conf.d/portscan/main.conf
134: 
135:     User overrides:
136:       /etc/nftban/nftban.conf.local
137: 
138:     Example override:
139:       PORTSCAN_THRESHOLD="5"           # Lower threshold (aggressive)
140:       PORTSCAN_BAN_TYPE="permanent"    # Permanent bans
141:       PORTSCAN_AUTO_BAN="false"        # Monitoring mode (no bans)
142: 
143: PROFILE SELECTION:
144:     Select a pre-configured profile based on server role:
145: 
146:       nftban profile select
147: 
148:     Profile examples:
149:       • Web Server:    10 ports in 5 min, 1-hour temp ban
150:       • Mail Server:   8 ports in 3 min, 2-hour temp ban
151:       • Database:      5 ports in 2 min, permanent ban
152:       • Development:   No auto-ban (monitoring only)
153:       • Maximum:       3 ports in 1 min, permanent ban
154: 
155: EXAMPLES:
156:     # Enable port scan detection
157:     sudo nftban portscan enable
158: 
159:     # Disable port scan detection
160:     sudo nftban portscan disable
161: 
162:     # Show detection status
163:     nftban portscan status
164: 
165:     # Run manual check (parse logs)
166:     sudo nftban portscan check
167: 
168:     # Show detected scans
169:     nftban portscan history
170: 
171:     # Test detection rules
172:     nftban portscan test
173: 
174: WHITELIST:
175:     Create whitelist for monitoring/security tools:
176:       /etc/nftban/portscan_whitelist.conf
177: 
178:     Format (one IP/CIDR per line):
179:       # Monitoring tools
180:       192.168.1.100
181:       10.0.0.0/8        # Internal network
182:       203.0.113.0/24    # Security scanner
183: 
184: LOG FILES:
185:     Detection logs: /var/log/nftban/portscan.log
186:     Statistics: /var/lib/nftban/portscan/stats.json
187:     Tracking database: /var/lib/nftban/portscan/tracker.db
188: 
189: REQUIREMENTS:
190:     • Root privileges (for enable/disable commands)
191:     • nftables >= 0.9.0
192:     • Kernel logging enabled
193: 
194: SEE ALSO:
195:     nftban ddos help         - DDoS protection help
196:     nftban profile help      - Profile selection help
197:     nftban ban help          - Ban management help
198: 
199: HELP
200: }
