<file path="cmd/nftban-ui/DEV_MODE.md">
  1: # NFTBan UI Development Mode
  2: 
  3: ## Problem
  4: 
  5: The NFTBan Web GUI uses Go's `//go:embed` directive to compile static files (HTML, JavaScript, CSS) directly into the binary. This creates a **single self-contained executable**, which is great for production deployment.
  6: 
  7: However, during development, this approach requires **rebuilding the entire binary** every time you make changes to HTML, JS, or CSS files. This is time-consuming and frustrating.
  8: 
  9: ## Solution: `--dev` Flag
 10: 
 11: The `--dev` flag enables **development mode**, which serves static files directly from disk instead of the embedded filesystem. This means:
 12: 
 13: - ✅ **No rebuild needed** for HTML/JS/CSS changes
 14: - ✅ **Just edit and refresh** your browser
 15: - ✅ **Faster development iteration**
 16: - ✅ **Production builds** still use embedded files (single binary)
 17: 
 18: ## Usage
 19: 
 20: ### Production Mode (Default)
 21: 
 22: Uses embedded files compiled into the binary:
 23: 
 24: ```bash
 25: ./nftban-ui
 26: ```
 27: 
 28: ### Development Mode
 29: 
 30: Serves files from disk (no rebuild needed for HTML/JS/CSS changes):
 31: 
 32: ```bash
 33: ./nftban-ui --dev
 34: ```
 35: 
 36: ## How It Works
 37: 
 38: ### readFile() Helper Function
 39: 
 40: ```go
 41: func readFile(path string) ([]byte, error) {
 42:     if isDevelopmentMode {
 43:         // Development mode: read from disk
 44:         return os.ReadFile(path)
 45:     }
 46:     // Production mode: read from embedded FS
 47:     return embedFS.ReadFile(path)
 48: }
 49: ```
 50: 
 51: ### File Paths
 52: 
 53: When running in dev mode, files are served from:
 54: 
 55: ```
 56: <project-root>/cmd/nftban-ui/web/static/
 57: ```
 58: 
 59: You must run `nftban-ui --dev` from the directory containing the `web/` folder.
 60: 
 61: ## Development Workflow
 62: 
 63: ### 1. Build Once
 64: 
 65: ```bash
 66: cd /path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui
 67: CGO_ENABLED=1 go build -o nftban-ui .
 68: ```
 69: 
 70: ### 2. Run in Dev Mode
 71: 
 72: ```bash
 73: ./nftban-ui --dev
 74: ```
 75: 
 76: You'll see:
 77: ```
 78: [DEV MODE] Serving files from disk (cmd/nftban-ui/web/) - No rebuild needed for HTML/JS/CSS changes!
 79: ```
 80: 
 81: ### 3. Edit HTML/JS/CSS Files
 82: 
 83: ```bash
 84: # Edit any file in web/static/
 85: vim web/static/pages/portscan.html
 86: vim web/static/js/page-loader.js
 87: vim web/static/css/nftban-modern.css
 88: ```
 89: 
 90: ### 4. Refresh Browser
 91: 
 92: Just hit **F5** or **Ctrl+Shift+R** (hard refresh) - changes appear immediately!
 93: 
 94: ### 5. When Done: Production Build
 95: 
 96: Before deploying to production, rebuild without `--dev` to embed files:
 97: 
 98: ```bash
 99: CGO_ENABLED=1 go build -o nftban-ui .
100: # Files are now embedded in the binary
101: ```
102: 
103: ## Files Using Dev Mode
104: 
105: The following handlers support dev mode:
106: 
107: - `/` and `/index.html` - Main page
108: - `/static/pages/*.html` - Modular pages (dashboard, portscan, ddos, fail2ban, etc.)
109: - `/static/js/page-loader.js` - Dynamic page loader
110: 
111: ## Security Considerations
112: 
113: ### File Permissions (FHS Compliance)
114: 
115: All files maintain proper FHS permissions:
116: 
117: ```bash
118: # Files owned by nftban user/group
119: chown -R nftban:nftban /path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui/web/
120: 
121: # Secure permissions
122: chmod 755 /path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui/web/
123: chmod 644 /path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui/web/static/**/*
124: ```
125: 
126: ### Production Deployment
127: 
128: **IMPORTANT:** Never use `--dev` in production!
129: 
130: - ✅ Production: Embedded files (single binary, no disk access)
131: - ❌ Development: Disk files (requires source directory)
132: 
133: ## Benefits
134: 
135: ### Before (Embedded Only)
136: 
137: ```bash
138: # Edit HTML file
139: vim web/static/pages/portscan.html
140: 
141: # Rebuild (slow!)
142: go build -o nftban-ui .     # ~10-30 seconds
143: 
144: # Deploy
145: systemctl restart nftban-ui
146: 
147: # Repeat for every change 😫
148: ```
149: 
150: ### After (With --dev Flag)
151: 
152: ```bash
153: # Build ONCE
154: go build -o nftban-ui .
155: 
156: # Run in dev mode
157: ./nftban-ui --dev
158: 
159: # Edit HTML file
160: vim web/static/pages/portscan.html
161: 
162: # Refresh browser (instant!)  # ✨ No rebuild needed! ✨
163: 
164: # Repeat edits as many times as needed 😊
165: ```
166: 
167: ## Examples
168: 
169: ### Editing Portscan Page
170: 
171: ```bash
172: # 1. Start dev mode
173: cd /path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui
174: ./nftban-ui --dev
175: 
176: # 2. Edit portscan page
177: vim web/static/pages/portscan.html
178: 
179: # 3. Save and refresh browser
180: # Changes appear immediately!
181: 
182: # 4. Edit page loader
183: vim web/static/js/page-loader.js
184: 
185: # 5. Refresh again
186: # Changes appear immediately!
187: ```
188: 
189: ### Switching Between Modes
190: 
191: ```bash
192: # Development mode (read from disk)
193: ./nftban-ui --dev
194: 
195: # Production mode (read from embedded FS)
196: ./nftban-ui
197: ```
198: 
199: ## Troubleshooting
200: 
201: ### Files Not Updating
202: 
203: **Problem:** Changes don't appear after browser refresh
204: 
205: **Solution:** Hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R) to bypass browser cache
206: 
207: ### 404 Not Found
208: 
209: **Problem:** Static files return 404 errors
210: 
211: **Solution:** Ensure you're running from the directory containing `web/`:
212: 
213: ```bash
214: cd /path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui
215: ./nftban-ui --dev
216: ```
217: 
218: ### Permission Denied
219: 
220: **Problem:** Cannot read files from disk
221: 
222: **Solution:** Check file permissions:
223: 
224: ```bash
225: chmod 644 web/static/pages/*.html
226: chmod 755 web/static/pages/
227: ```
228: 
229: ## Systemd Service with Dev Mode
230: 
231: To run the systemd service in dev mode:
232: 
233: ```bash
234: # Edit service file
235: vim /etc/systemd/system/nftban-ui.service
236: 
237: # Change ExecStart to:
238: ExecStart=/usr/sbin/nftban-ui --dev
239: 
240: # But ensure WorkingDirectory is set:
241: WorkingDirectory=/path/to/nftban/cmd/nftban-ui
242: 
243: # Reload and restart
244: systemctl daemon-reload
245: systemctl restart nftban-ui
246: ```
247: 
248: **⚠️ WARNING:** Only use this for development servers, never in production!
249: 
250: ## Summary
251: 
252: | Feature | Production Mode | Development Mode |
253: |---------|----------------|------------------|
254: | **Command** | `./nftban-ui` | `./nftban-ui --dev` |
255: | **File Source** | Embedded in binary | Read from disk |
256: | **Rebuild Needed** | Yes (for every change) | No (just refresh browser) |
257: | **Performance** | Faster (embedded) | Slightly slower (disk I/O) |
258: | **Deployment** | Single binary | Requires source directory |
259: | **Use Case** | Production | Development |
260: 
261: ## Related Files
262: 
263: - `cmd/nftban-ui/main.go` - Contains `readFile()` helper and `--dev` flag
264: - `cmd/nftban-ui/web/static/pages/*.html` - Modular HTML pages
265: - `cmd/nftban-ui/web/static/js/page-loader.js` - Dynamic page loader
266: - `cmd/nftban-ui/web/static/index.html` - Main entry point
267: 
268: ## Questions?
269: 
270: See commit message for implementation details:
271: ```
272: feat(ui): Add --dev flag to avoid rebuilds for HTML/JS/CSS changes
273: ```
274: 
275: Resolves: "why to be build?" development pain point
</file>

<file path="cmd/nftban-ui/enable-dev-mode.sh">
 1: #!/usr/bin/env bash
 2: # =============================================================================
 3: # Enable Development Mode for nftban-ui.service
 4: # =============================================================================
 5: # This script configures the nftban-ui systemd service to run in development
 6: # mode, which serves files from disk instead of embedded FS.
 7: #
 8: # WARNING: Only use this on development servers, NEVER in production!
 9: # =============================================================================
10: 
11: set -Eeuo pipefail
12: 
13: # Colors
14: GREEN='\033[0;32m'
15: YELLOW='\033[1;33m'
16: RED='\033[0;31m'
17: NC='\033[0m' # No Color
18: 
19: echo -e "${YELLOW}🔧 Enabling Development Mode for nftban-ui${NC}"
20: echo ""
21: 
22: # Check if running as root
23: if [[ $EUID -ne 0 ]]; then
24:    echo -e "${RED}❌ This script must be run as root${NC}"
25:    exit 1
26: fi
27: 
28: # Service file path
29: SERVICE_FILE="/etc/systemd/system/nftban-ui.service"
30: OVERRIDE_DIR="/etc/systemd/system/nftban-ui.service.d"
31: DEV_OVERRIDE_FILE="$OVERRIDE_DIR/dev-mode.conf"
32: 
33: # Check if service exists
34: if [[ ! -f "$SERVICE_FILE" ]]; then
35:     echo -e "${RED}❌ Service file not found: $SERVICE_FILE${NC}"
36:     exit 1
37: fi
38: 
39: # Create override directory if it doesn't exist
40: mkdir -p "$OVERRIDE_DIR"
41: 
42: # Get source directory (default to /root/nftban-dev for backwards compatibility)
43: DEV_SOURCE_DIR="${NFTBAN_DEV_SOURCE_DIR:-/root/nftban-dev}"
44: 
45: # Create dev mode override
46: cat > "$DEV_OVERRIDE_FILE" <<EOF
47: [Service]
48: # Development mode: serve files from disk (no rebuild needed for HTML/JS/CSS)
49: WorkingDirectory=$DEV_SOURCE_DIR/cmd/nftban-ui
50: ExecStart=
51: ExecStart=$DEV_SOURCE_DIR/cmd/nftban-ui/nftban-ui --dev
52: 
53: # Log dev mode startup
54: StandardOutput=journal
55: StandardError=journal
56: EOF
57: 
58: echo -e "${GREEN}✅ Created dev mode override: $DEV_OVERRIDE_FILE${NC}"
59: 
60: # Reload systemd
61: systemctl daemon-reload
62: echo -e "${GREEN}✅ Reloaded systemd daemon${NC}"
63: 
64: # Restart service
65: systemctl restart nftban-ui
66: echo -e "${GREEN}✅ Restarted nftban-ui service${NC}"
67: 
68: # Show status
69: echo ""
70: echo -e "${YELLOW}📊 Service Status:${NC}"
71: systemctl status nftban-ui --no-pager -l | head -15
72: 
73: echo ""
74: echo -e "${GREEN}🎉 Development mode enabled!${NC}"
75: echo ""
76: echo -e "${YELLOW}Now you can:${NC}"
77: echo "  1. Edit HTML/JS/CSS files in $DEV_SOURCE_DIR/cmd/nftban-ui/web/"
78: echo "  2. Refresh your browser (Ctrl+Shift+R)"
79: echo "  3. See changes immediately - NO REBUILD NEEDED!"
80: echo ""
81: echo -e "${YELLOW}To check logs:${NC}"
82: echo "  journalctl -u nftban-ui -f"
83: echo ""
