787: 
788: ## Troubleshooting
789: 
790: ### No Statistics Available
791: 
792: **Symptoms:** `sid stats` shows 0 SIDs, empty output
793: 
794: **Solutions:**
795: ```bash
796: # 1. Verify Suricata is running
797: sudo systemctl status suricata
798: 
799: # 2. Check eve.json exists and has data
800: ls -la /var/log/suricata/eve.json
801: tail -f /var/log/suricata/eve.json | jq 'select(.event_type=="alert")'
802: 
803: # 3. Start stats collector
804: sudo systemctl start nftban-suricata-stats
805: sudo journalctl -u nftban-suricata-stats -f
806: 
807: # 4. Generate some traffic to trigger alerts
808: curl http://localhost/
809: ```
810: 
811: ### Services Not Detected
812: 
813: **Symptoms:** `scan` shows no services or missing expected services
814: 
815: **Solutions:**
816: ```bash
817: # 1. Verify services are actually running
818: ss -tlnp | grep -E ':(80|443|22|3306|25|53)'
819: 
820: # 2. Check firewall not blocking localhost
821: sudo iptables -L INPUT -n | grep lo
822: sudo ip6tables -L INPUT -n | grep lo
823: 
824: # 3. Use deep scan for better detection
825: nftban suricata scan deep
826: 
827: # 4. Manually edit local.conf if needed
828: sudo vi /etc/nftban/suricata/config/suricata.local.conf
829: # Add: enabled_categories = http,ssh,mysql
830: ```
831: 
832: ### Custom Rule Validation Failed
833: 
834: **Symptoms:** Rule rejected with syntax errors
835: 
836: **Common Issues:**
837: ```bash
838: # Missing required fields
839: # ✗ BAD: alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"Test";)
840: # ✓ GOOD: alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"Test"; sid:9000000; rev:1;)
841: 
842: # SID out of range
843: # ✗ BAD: sid:1000000;
844: # ✓ GOOD: sid:9000000;
845: 
846: # Unbalanced parentheses
847: # ✗ BAD: alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"Test"; sid:9000000; rev:1;
848: # ✓ GOOD: alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"Test"; sid:9000000; rev:1;)
849: 
850: # Test manually with Suricata
851: echo 'alert tcp any any -> any 80 (msg:"Test"; sid:9000000; rev:1;)' | suricata -T -S -
852: ```
853: 
854: ### Rules Not Reducing
855: 
856: **Symptoms:** `rules stats` shows 100% or no reduction
857: 
858: **Solutions:**
859: ```bash
860: # 1. Verify scan was run
861: cat /etc/nftban/suricata/config/suricata.auto.conf
862: # Should show: enabled_categories = http,ssh,...
863: 
864: # 2. Check effective.conf
865: cat /etc/nftban/suricata/config/suricata.effective.conf
866: # Should merge local + auto
867: 
868: # 3. Regenerate rules list
869: nftban suricata rules generate
870: 
871: # 4. Verify enabled.list created
872: wc -l /etc/nftban/suricata/config/enabled.list
873: ```
874: 
875: ### Permission Denied Errors
876: 
877: **Symptoms:** Commands fail with permission errors
878: 
879: **Solutions:**
880: ```bash
881: # 1. Use sudo for root commands
882: sudo nftban suricata <command>
883: 
884: # 2. Check directory permissions
885: sudo ls -la /etc/nftban/suricata/
886: sudo chown -R root:root /etc/nftban/suricata
887: sudo chmod 755 /etc/nftban/suricata
888: 
889: # 3. Verify nftban-core is executable
890: sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/nftban-core
891: ```
892: 
893: ### Recommendations Show Nothing
894: 
895: **Symptoms:** `recommend` shows "No recommendations"
896: 
897: **Expected Behavior:** This is normal if:
898: - Suricata recently started (no alerts yet)
899: - All rules performing optimally
900: - Not enough data collected (wait 24h)
901: 
902: **To Generate Test Data:**
903: ```bash
904: # Trigger some alerts for testing
905: # (safely, on your own system)
906: 
907: # Start stats collector
908: sudo systemctl start nftban-suricata-stats
909: 
910: # Wait for some alerts
911: sleep 300
912: 
913: # Check again
914: nftban suricata recommend
915: ```
916: 
