<file path="CONTRIBUTING.md">
  1: # Contributing to NFTBan
  2: 
  3: Thank you for your interest in contributing to NFTBAN! This document provides guidelines for contributing.
  4: 
  5: ## About the Project
  6: 
  7: **NFTBAN** is an enterprise-grade firewall management engine built on Linux nftables. The name stands for **NFTables BAN actions**, emphasizing the system's foundation on native nftables technology for high-performance, kernel-level packet filtering.
  8: 
  9: ## Project Terminology
 10: 
 11: When writing documentation or code:
 12: 
 13: - **NFTBAN** (all caps) — Project name in formal contexts, marketing materials, and when emphasizing the acronym
 14: - **NFTBan** (title case) — Stylized form for README headers and user-facing documentation
 15: - **nftban** (lowercase) — Command name, binary name, file paths, and code references
 16: - **nftables** — Always lowercase (the underlying Linux kernel technology)
 17: 
 18: **Example usage:**
 19: - ✅ "NFTBAN is built on nftables technology"
 20: - ✅ "Run the `nftban` command to manage firewall rules"
 21: - ✅ "See the NFTBan documentation for details"
 22: 
 23: ## Code of Conduct
 24: 
 25: Please read our [Code of Conduct](.github/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) before contributing.
 26: 
 27: ## How to Contribute
 28: 
 29: ### Reporting Bugs
 30: 
 31: 1. Check existing [issues](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/issues) first
 32: 2. Use the bug report template
 33: 3. Include:
 34:    - NFTBan version (`nftban version`)
 35:    - OS and version (`cat /etc/os-release`)
 36:    - Steps to reproduce
 37:    - Expected vs actual behavior
 38:    - Relevant logs (`/var/log/nftban/`)
 39: 
 40: ### Suggesting Features
 41: 
 42: 1. Check existing issues and discussions
 43: 2. Use the feature request template
 44: 3. Explain the use case and benefit
 45: 
 46: ### Pull Requests
 47: 
 48: 1. Fork the repository
 49: 2. Create a feature branch: `git checkout -b feature/your-feature`
 50: 3. Make your changes
 51: 4. Run tests: `nftban smoke`
 52: 5. Commit with clear messages
 53: 6. Push and create a PR
 54: 
 55: ## Development Setup
 56: 
 57: ### Prerequisites
 58: 
 59: - Go 1.22+
 60: - Bash 4.4+
 61: - nftables
 62: - Linux (Rocky/Alma/Ubuntu/Debian)
 63: 
 64: ### Building
 65: 
 66: ```bash
 67: # Clone repository
 68: git clone https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban.git
 69: cd nftban
 70: 
 71: # Build Go binaries
 72: ./build.sh
 73: 
 74: # Install for testing
 75: sudo ./install.sh
 76: ```
 77: 
 78: ### Project Structure
 79: 
 80: ```
 81: nftban/
 82: ├── cli/                    # Bash CLI
 83: │   └── lib/nftban/
 84: │       ├── core/          # Core functionality
 85: │       ├── cli/           # Command handlers
 86: │       ├── helpers/       # Utility functions
 87: │       └── setup/         # Installation helpers
 88: ├── cmd/                    # Go binaries
 89: │   ├── nftban-core/       # Main Go binary
 90: │   ├── nftban-api-server/ # REST API
 91: │   └── nftban-ui/         # Web interface
 92: ├── pkg/                    # Go packages
 93: ├── install/               # Installation scripts
 94: ├── packaging/             # RPM/DEB specs
 95: └── docs/                  # Documentation
 96: ```
 97: 
 98: ## Coding Standards
 99: 
100: ### Bash
101: 
102: - Use `set -Eeuo pipefail` at the top
103: - Quote all variables: `"$var"`
104: - Use `[[` for conditionals
105: - Add comments for complex logic
106: - Follow existing naming conventions
107: 
108: ### Go
109: 
110: - Run `go fmt` before committing
111: - Run `go vet` and fix warnings
112: - Use meaningful variable names
113: - Add tests for new functionality
114: 
115: ### Commits
116: 
117: - Use conventional commits:
118:   - `feat:` New feature
119:   - `fix:` Bug fix
120:   - `docs:` Documentation
121:   - `refactor:` Code refactoring
122:   - `test:` Adding tests
123:   - `chore:` Maintenance
124: 
125: ### Examples
126: 
127: ```bash
128: # Good commit messages
129: feat(cli): Add IP search across all sets
130: fix(geoban): Handle empty country list gracefully
131: docs: Update installation guide for Rocky 9
132: 
133: # Bad commit messages
134: fixed stuff
135: update
136: wip
137: ```
138: 
139: ## Testing
140: 
141: ### Running Tests
142: 
143: ```bash
144: # Quick smoke test
145: nftban smoke
146: 
147: # Full test suite
148: ./tests/test_all_commands.sh
149: 
150: # ShellCheck (bash linting)
151: shellcheck cli/lib/nftban/**/*.sh
152: 
153: # Go tests
154: go test ./...
155: ```
156: 
157: ### Test Before PR
158: 
159: 1. All commands work: `nftban smoke`
160: 2. ShellCheck passes (warnings OK)
161: 3. Go builds without errors
162: 4. No regressions in existing functionality
163: 
164: ## Questions?
165: 
166: - Open a [discussion](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/discussions)
167: - Check [documentation](docs/)
168: - Review [support guide](.github/SUPPORT.md)
169: 
170: ## License
171: 
172: By contributing, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the MPL-2.0 License.
</file>

