1431:     3. Investigate: nftban suricata sid info <SID>
1432:     4. Apply fixes: disable/modify rules as needed
1433:     5. Monitor: nftban suricata sid top
1434: 
1435: ANALYSIS PATTERNS:
1436:     - False Positive: 100+ triggers from 1-3 sources
1437:     - Noise: 1000+ triggers, widespread sources, low ratio
1438:     - Drop Mode: Attack patterns from many sources
1439:     - Disable: 10,000+ triggers, very recent activity
1440: 
1441: NOTES:
1442:     - Recommendations based on current statistics
1443:     - Run after collecting data for at least 24 hours
1444:     - Review recommendations before applying changes
1445:     - Some "noisy" rules may be legitimate for your environment
1446: 
1447: EOF
1448:             ;;
1449:     esac
1450: }
1451: 
1452: # =============================================================================
1453: # HELP
1454: # =============================================================================
1455: 
1456: cmd_suricata_help() {
1457:     cat << 'EOF'
1458: 
1459: 🛡️  NFTBan - Suricata IDS Management
1460: 
1461: USAGE:
1462:     nftban suricata <command>
1463: 
1464: COMMANDS:
1465:     install     Install Suricata IDS (automated)
1466:     enable      Enable and start Suricata service
1467:     disable     Stop and disable Suricata service
1468:     status      Show Suricata status and recent alerts
1469:     profile     Manage performance profiles (see: nftban suricata profile help)
1470:     scan        Scan services and auto-configure (see: nftban suricata scan help)
1471:     services    Manage service configuration (see: nftban suricata services help)
1472:     rules       Manage Suricata rules (see: nftban suricata rules help)
1473:     sid         SID statistics and analysis (see: nftban suricata sid help)
1474:     custom      Manage custom rules (see: nftban suricata custom help)
1475:     recommend   Get intelligent rule recommendations (see: nftban suricata recommend help)
1476:     help        Show this help message
1477: 
1478: INSTALLATION PROCESS:
1479:     1. Checks for package availability (EPEL/APT)
1480:     2. Installs from packages OR compiles from source
1481:     3. Downloads ET/Open ruleset (free)
1482:     4. Configures for NFTBan integration
1483:     5. Sets up systemd service
1484: 
1485: EXAMPLES:
1486:     # Full automated setup (one command):
1487:     nftban suricata install
1488:     nftban suricata enable
1489: 
1490:     # Check status:
1491:     nftban suricata status
1492: 
1493:     # Update rules:
1494:     nftban suricata rules update
1495: 
1496:     # View live alerts:
1497:     tail -f /var/log/suricata/eve.json | jq 'select(.event_type=="alert")'
1498: 
1499: REQUIREMENTS:
1500:     - Root privileges (sudo)
1501:     - EPEL repository (RHEL/Rocky) or standard repos (Debian/Ubuntu)
1502:     - 2+ cores, 2+ GB RAM recommended
1503:     - Python 3 + pip (for suricata-update)
1504: 
1505: PERFORMANCE:
1506:     - CPU: 10-30% of 1 core (medium traffic)
1507:     - RAM: 300-800 MB typical
1508:     - Optimized for VPS/cloud environments
1509: 
1510: DOCUMENTATION:
1511:     - Suricata: https://suricata.io/
1512:     - NFTBan Suricata guide: https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/Suricata-Integration
1513: 
1514: EOF
1515: }
1516: 
1517: # =============================================================================
1518: # COMMAND ROUTER
1519: # =============================================================================
1520: 
1521: nftban_cmd_suricata() {
1522:     local action="${1:-help}"
1523:     shift || true
1524: 
1525:     case "$action" in
1526:         install)
1527:             cmd_suricata_install "$@"
1528:             ;;
1529:         enable)
1530:             cmd_suricata_enable "$@"
1531:             ;;
1532:         disable)
1533:             cmd_suricata_disable "$@"
1534:             ;;
1535:         status)
1536:             cmd_suricata_status "$@"
1537:             ;;
1538:         rules)
1539:             cmd_suricata_rules "$@"
1540:             ;;
1541:         profile)
1542:             cmd_suricata_profile "$@"
1543:             ;;
1544:         scan)
1545:             cmd_suricata_scan "$@"
1546:             ;;
1547:         services)
1548:             cmd_suricata_services "$@"
1549:             ;;
1550:         sid)
1551:             cmd_suricata_sid "$@"
1552:             ;;
1553:         custom)
