  1: #!/usr/bin/env bash
  2: # =============================================================================
  3: # NFTBan - Wiki Generator (Auditor View)
  4: # =============================================================================
  5: # SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
  6: # Purpose: Generate CLI Commands Reference for auditors (read-only)
  7: #
  8: # Usage: ./scripts/generate-wiki-auditor.sh > wiki/CLI-Commands-Reference-Auditor.md
  9: # Output: Markdown wiki page with auditor-visible commands only
 10: # =============================================================================
 11: 
 12: set -euo pipefail
 13: 
 14: # Source central config for canonical paths (NO HARDCODED FALLBACKS)
 15: # shellcheck source=/etc/nftban/nftban.conf
 16: [[ -f "${NFTBAN_CONFIG_DIR:-/etc/nftban}/nftban.conf" ]] && source "${NFTBAN_CONFIG_DIR:-/etc/nftban}/nftban.conf"
 17: 
 18: # Determine registry location (installed vs development)
 19: if [[ -f "${NFTBAN_CONFIG_DIR:-/etc/nftban}/commands.registry.yml" ]]; then
 20:     # Installed location (FHS compliant)
 21:     REGISTRY="${NFTBAN_CONFIG_DIR:-/etc/nftban}/commands.registry.yml"
 22: else
 23:     # Development location (relative to script)
 24:     SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
 25:     PROJECT_ROOT="$(cd "$SCRIPT_DIR/.." && pwd)"
 26:     REGISTRY="${PROJECT_ROOT}/commands.registry.yml"
 27: fi
 28: 
 29: # =============================================================================
 30: # CHECK DEPENDENCIES
 31: # =============================================================================
 32: 
 33: if ! command -v yq &>/dev/null; then
 34:     echo "ERROR: yq is required for YAML parsing" >&2
 35:     exit 1
 36: fi
 37: 
 38: # =============================================================================
 39: # WIKI HEADER
 40: # =============================================================================
 41: 
 42: cat <<'EOF'
 43: # NFTBan CLI Commands Reference (Auditor View)
 44: 
 45: **Read-only reference for compliance, audit, and security operations team**
 46: 
 47: > **Auto-generated from `commands.registry.yml`** - Do not edit manually
 48: 
 49: ---
 50: 
 51: ## Auditor Profile
 52: 
 53: This documentation shows **read-only commands** available to users in the `nftban-auditor` group.
 54: 
 55: **What Auditors Can Do:**
 56: - ✅ View system status and health
 57: - ✅ Read reports, statistics, and metrics
 58: - ✅ Search logs and check IP status
 59: - ✅ View configuration (read-only)
 60: - ❌ Cannot modify firewall rules
 61: - ❌ Cannot ban/unban IPs
 62: - ❌ Cannot enable/disable services
 63: - ❌ Cannot change system configuration
 64: 
 65: ---
 66: 
 67: ## Quick Examples
 68: 
 69: ```bash
 70: # Check system status
 71: nftban status
 72: nftban status --json
 73: 
 74: # View health and diagnostics
 75: nftban health check
 76: nftban health summary
 77: 
 78: # Search for IP activity
 79: nftban search 1.2.3.4
 80: nftban check 1.2.3.4
 81: 
 82: # View current bans and whitelist
 83: nftban list banned
 84: nftban list whitelist
 85: 
 86: # Generate compliance reports
 87: nftban report generate
 88: nftban stats top
 89: 
 90: # View service status
 91: nftban services status --json
 92: ```
 93: 
 94: ---
 95: 
 96: ## Global Options (Auditor-Safe)
 97: 
 98: | Option | Description |
 99: |--------|-------------|
100: | `--json` | Output machine-readable JSON |
101: | `--help`, `-h` | Command-specific help |
102: 
103: **Note:** `--dry-run` is not needed for auditors (all commands are read-only)
104: 
105: ---
106: 
107: EOF
108: 
109: # =============================================================================
110: # FILTER FUNCTION
111: # =============================================================================
112: 
113: is_auditor_visible() {
114:     local cmd="$1"
115: 
116:     # Check if auditor is in audience array
117:     local audience
118:     audience=$(yq -r ".\"$cmd\".audience[]?" "$REGISTRY" 2>/dev/null || echo "")
119: 
120:     echo "$audience" | grep -q "auditor"
121: }
122: 
123: # =============================================================================
124: # TASK GROUP GENERATOR (FILTERED)
125: # =============================================================================
126: 
127: generate_auditor_group() {
128:     local category="$1"
129:     local title="$2"
130:     local icon="$3"
131:     local description="$4"
132: 
133:     # Get ALL commands for this category
134:     local all_commands
135:     all_commands=$(yq -r "
136:         to_entries |
137:         map(select(.key != \"_metadata\" and .value.category == \"$category\")) |
138:         map(.key) |
139:         .[]
140:     " "$REGISTRY" 2>/dev/null | sort)
141: 
142:     # Filter for auditor visibility
143:     local auditor_commands=()
144:     for cmd in $all_commands; do
145:         if is_auditor_visible "$cmd"; then
146:             auditor_commands+=("$cmd")
147:         fi
148:     done
149: 
150:     # Skip empty groups
151:     [[ ${#auditor_commands[@]} -eq 0 ]] && return
152: 
153:     cat <<EOF
154: 
155: ## $icon  $title
156: 
157: **$description**
158: 
159: | Command | Description | JSON |
160: |---------|-------------|------|
161: EOF
162: 
163:     for cmd in "${auditor_commands[@]}"; do
164:         local desc has_json
165:         desc=$(yq -r ".\"$cmd\".description" "$REGISTRY")
166:         has_json=$(yq -r ".\"$cmd\".has_json" "$REGISTRY")
167: 
168:         local json_icon
169:         [[ "$has_json" == "true" ]] && json_icon="✅" || json_icon="❌"
170: 
171:         echo "| \`$cmd\` | $desc | $json_icon |"
172:     done
173: 
174:     echo ""
175:     echo "### Command Details"
176:     echo ""
177: 
178:     # Generate detailed documentation
179:     for cmd in "${auditor_commands[@]}"; do
180:         local desc has_json examples
181:         desc=$(yq -r ".\"$cmd\".description" "$REGISTRY")
182:         has_json=$(yq -r ".\"$cmd\".has_json" "$REGISTRY")
183: 
184:         # Get examples array
185:         examples=$(yq -r ".\"$cmd\".examples[]?" "$REGISTRY" 2>/dev/null || echo "")
186: 
187:         cat <<EOF
188: 
189: #### \`nftban $cmd\`
190: 
191: **Description:** $desc
192: **JSON Support:** $has_json
193: **Read-Only:** ✅ Safe for auditors
194: 
195: EOF
196: 
197:         if [[ -n "$examples" ]]; then
198:             echo "**Examples:**"
199:             echo '```bash'
200:             echo "$examples"
201:             echo '```'
202:             echo ""
203:         fi
204:     done
205: }
206: 
207: # =============================================================================
208: # GENERATE FILTERED GROUPS
209: # =============================================================================
210: 
211: generate_auditor_group "setup_discovery" "Setup & Discovery" "🛠️" "System diagnostics and health checks"
212: generate_auditor_group "immediate_action" "Immediate Action" "⚡" "Read-only status checks"
213: generate_auditor_group "active_protection" "Active Protection" "🧱" "View protection module status"
214: generate_auditor_group "infrastructure" "Infrastructure" "⚙️" "Configuration viewing"
215: generate_auditor_group "intelligence_reporting" "Intelligence & Reporting" "📊" "Reports, stats, and metrics"
216: generate_auditor_group "developer_sysadmin" "Developer / SysAdmin" "🧪" "Diagnostic tools"
217: 
218: # =============================================================================
219: # FOOTER
220: # =============================================================================
221: 
222: cat <<'EOF'
223: 
224: ---
225: 
226: ## Compliance Use Cases
227: 
228: ### Security Audit
229: 
230: ```bash
231: # 1. Verify firewall structure
232: nftban validate all --json
233: 
234: # 2. Check service status
235: nftban services status --json
236: 
237: # 3. Review current bans
238: nftban list banned --json
239: 
240: # 4. Generate compliance report
241: nftban report generate
242: ```
243: 
244: ### Incident Investigation
245: 
246: ```bash
247: # 1. Check system health
248: nftban health check
249: 
250: # 2. Search for IP in question
251: nftban search 1.2.3.4 --json
252: 
253: # 3. Check if IP is currently blocked
254: nftban check 1.2.3.4 --json
255: 
256: # 4. View recent statistics
257: nftban stats recent --json
258: ```
259: 
260: ### Regular Monitoring
261: 
262: ```bash
263: # Daily status check
264: nftban status --json > /tmp/nftban-status-$(date +%Y%m%d).json
265: 
266: # Weekly report generation
267: nftban report generate --json
268: 
269: # Monthly metrics export
270: nftban stats export --json > /var/audit/nftban-monthly.json
271: ```
272: 
273: ---
274: 
275: ## JSON Output for Automation
276: 
277: All auditor commands support `--json` for easy parsing and integration with SIEM/logging platforms.
278: 
279: **Standard JSON Schema:**
280: ```json
281: {
282:   "success": true,
283:   "timestamp": "2025-12-31T12:34:56Z",
284:   "data": {
285:     ...command-specific data...
286:   }
287: }
288: ```
289: 
290: **Example - Automated Compliance Check:**
291: ```bash
292: #!/bin/bash
293: # Daily NFTBan compliance check
294: 
295: REPORT_FILE="/var/audit/nftban-$(date +%Y%m%d).json"
296: 
297: # Collect status
298: nftban status --json > "$REPORT_FILE"
299: 
300: # Append services status
301: nftban services status --json >> "$REPORT_FILE"
302: 
303: # Append current bans
304: nftban list banned --json >> "$REPORT_FILE"
305: 
306: # Send to SIEM
307: curl -X POST https://siem.example.com/api/logs \
308:   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
309:   -d @"$REPORT_FILE"
310: ```
311: 
312: ---
313: 
314: ## Access Control
315: 
316: ### Group Membership
317: 
318: Auditors must be added to the `nftban-auditor` Linux group:
319: 
320: ```bash
321: # Add user to auditor group (requires root)
322: sudo usermod -a -G nftban-auditor username
323: 
324: # Verify membership
325: groups username
326: ```
327: 
328: ### Permissions
329: 
330: Auditor group has:
331: - ✅ Read access to `/var/log/nftban/`
332: - ✅ Read access to `/var/lib/nftban/reports/`
333: - ✅ Read access to configuration files (via polkit)
334: - ❌ No write access to firewall rules
335: - ❌ No service control permissions
336: 
337: ---
