<file path="SECURITY.md">
  1: # Security Policy
  2: 
  3: ## About NFTBAN
  4: 
  5: NFTBAN is an enterprise-grade firewall management engine built on Linux nftables. Security is foundational to our architecture, featuring Polkit-based privilege separation, systemd sandboxing, and strict input validation at all layers.
  6: 
  7: ## Reporting Security Vulnerabilities
  8: 
  9: We take security seriously and follow responsible disclosure practices. If you discover a security vulnerability in NFTBAN, please report it responsibly.
 10: 
 11: ### How to Report
 12: 
 13: **Please DO NOT report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub issues.**
 14: 
 15: Instead, please report security vulnerabilities by:
 16: 
 17: 1. **Email:** Send details to security@itcms.gr
 18: 2. **Subject:** Include "NFTBan Security:" prefix
 19: 3. **Details:** Include:
 20:    - Description of the vulnerability
 21:    - Steps to reproduce
 22:    - Potential impact
 23:    - Suggested fix (if available)
 24:    - Your contact information
 25: 
 26: ### What to Expect
 27: 
 28: - **Acknowledgment:** Within 48 hours
 29: - **Initial Assessment:** Within 7 days
 30: - **Status Updates:** Every 7-14 days until resolution
 31: - **Credit:** Public acknowledgment in release notes (if desired)
 32: 
 33: ### Security Update Process
 34: 
 35: 1. **Verification:** We confirm the vulnerability
 36: 2. **Fix Development:** Create and test patch
 37: 3. **Private Disclosure:** Notify affected users before public release
 38: 4. **Public Release:** Publish fix with security advisory
 39: 5. **CVE Assignment:** Request CVE if applicable
 40: 
 41: ### Supported Versions
 42: 
 43: | Version | Supported          |
 44: | ------- | ------------------ |
 45: | 1.0.x   | ✅ Full support    |
 46: | 0.32.x  | ⚠️ Security fixes only |
 47: | < 0.32  | ❌ Not supported   |
 48: 
 49: **Recommendation:** Always use the latest stable release (v1.0.x) for best security.
 50: 
 51: ### Security Features
 52: 
 53: NFTBan includes comprehensive security features:
 54: 
 55: - **FHS Auto-Heal** - Self-correcting file system permissions
 56: - **Polkit Integration** - Least-privilege service management
 57: - **Suricata IDS** - Real-time intrusion detection
 58: - **Threat Feeds** - Automated malicious IP blocking
 59: - **Geo-Blocking** - Country-based access control
 60: - **DDoS Protection** - Multi-layer attack mitigation
 61: 
 62: For complete security documentation, see:
 63: 
 64: - **[Security Architecture](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/Security-Architecture)** - NFTBan's security model
 65: - **[Security Operations Guide](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/Security-Operations-Guide)** - Hardening and operations
 66: - **[Groups and Permissions](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/Groups-and-Permissions)** - Access control
 67: 
 68: ### Known Security Advisories
 69: 
 70: #### CVE-2024-NFTBAN-001 - Rule Order Bypass (FIXED)
 71: 
 72: **Severity:** HIGH
 73: **Affected:** v0.32.5 and earlier
 74: **Fixed in:** v0.32.6 (2025-11-05)
 75: **Status:** ✅ Patched in v1.0+
 76: 
 77: **Issue:** Blacklist checks ran after port allow rules, allowing blacklisted IPs to bypass firewall.
 78: 
 79: **Action Required:**
 80: - Upgrade to v1.0.x (recommended)
 81: - Or upgrade to v0.32.6+ minimum
 82: - Verify fix: `nftban firewall check`
 83: 
 84: **Details:** See [Security Operations Guide](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/Security-Operations-Guide#security-advisories)
 85: 
 86: ### Security Best Practices
 87: 
 88: 1. **Keep Updated** - Run latest stable version
 89: 2. **Monitor Logs** - Review security events daily
 90: 3. **Enable Health Checks** - Automated system validation
 91: 4. **Use Threat Feeds** - Block known malicious IPs
 92: 5. **Harden SSH** - Disable passwords, use keys only
 93: 6. **Backup Regularly** - Automated daily backups
 94: 7. **Test Restores** - Verify backup integrity quarterly
 95: 
 96: See the **[Security Operations Guide](https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/wiki/Security-Operations-Guide)** for complete hardening procedures.
 97: 
 98: ### Scope
 99: 
100: This security policy applies to:
101: 
102: - NFTBan core system
103: - NFTBan CLI tools
104: - NFTBan Go binaries
105: - Official installation packages (RPM, DEB)
106: - Official documentation and scripts
107: 
108: ### Out of Scope
109: 
110: The following are **not** covered by this security policy:
111: 
112: - Third-party dependencies (report to upstream)
113: - User misconfigurations
114: - Physical server security
115: - Social engineering attacks
116: - Theoretical vulnerabilities without proof of concept
117: 
118: ### Hall of Fame
119: 
120: We recognize security researchers who responsibly disclose vulnerabilities:
121: 
122: *No vulnerabilities reported yet for v1.0+*
123: 
124: ### Contact
125: 
126: - **Security Email:** security@itcms.gr
127: - **GitHub Issues:** https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/issues (non-security only)
128: - **Discussions:** https://github.com/itcmsgr/nftban/discussions
129: 
130: ---
131: 
132: **Thank you for helping keep NFTBan secure!**
